# local python env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# personal photo: its EXIF pinpoints where the crew stayed — kept out of the
# public repo. The hotel coordinate it yielded is recorded in poster.py.
out/IMG_0496.JPG

# working renders (compare_offset.png is kept — it documents the offset)
out/proof.png
out/proof_true.png
out/proof_depth.png

# The depth-band edition of the sheet, 3.7 MB of PNG and 13.8 MB of PDF. Kept out
# because re-committing rendered output is what took this history to 510 MB once
# already, and the drawn-halo edition above is already carrying a tracked pair.
# Delete these two lines if the depth edition should be the one in the repo.
out/abaco_poster_depth_18x24_300dpi.png
out/abaco_poster_depth_18x24.pdf

# the square page for the photobook, in both water treatments and any dpi
out/photobook_*.png
out/proof_offset.png

# derived caches — regenerated from the committed geo/*.json, and pickles are
# Python-version specific
geo/*.pkl

# optional local override for P052/Lato when they aren't installed system-wide.
# Not redistributed here: P052 is AGPL-with-font-exception, Lato is OFL-1.1.
fonts/

# the crew's photo archives — 32 GB of zips, read in place by the map build and
# never unpacked. Source material, not source code.
photos/

# the map's build output: ~1 GB across ~5,000 files, all of it regenerable.
# Committing rendered output is what took this repo's history to 510 MB once.
site_build/

# the photo index: regenerable from photos/ in 4 s, and it carries 512 EXIF
# coordinates — the anchorages, and the hotel the crew slept in. Same reason
# out/IMG_0496.JPG is kept out.
out/photo_index.json
out/clock_fit.json
out/placed.json

# vendored MapLibre is committed (BSD-3, 1 MB, keeps the build offline and the
# site free of any CDN); node_modules is only ever a screenshot harness
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# reference material parked in out/ while labels were checked: the hand-drawn
# map of the Abacos the cay names were read from, a drone frame (EXIF and all),
# and an AI mock-up. Things to check against, not outputs to ship.
out/LOCALABACOMAP.jpg
out/DJI_0177 - cropped.JPG
out/Gemini_Generated_Image_*.png

# a review pair of the sheet, rendered to look at rather than to keep — the
# tracked pair above is the one the README points people to
out/review_poster_*

# the NTFS "downloaded from the internet" stream, which WSL shows as a file
*:Zone.Identifier
